Design by Me, reviews by Claude.

This is a specific definition of Mind.
Mind is a simple language that can write blog.

Symbol:
   L a text until `\n`, exclusive `\n`
   U a URL until `\n`, exclusive `\n`
   N a text until `\n`, exclusive `\n`,
     at least one visible char includes
   S(c) replace 1st char of `  ` into c

[Each Content belongs to nearest Topic before]
[Each Topic should have Contents]
[First Line should be Topic]
[Background is black]

Topic:
S(`#`)N a topic bloder title, 1 line,
        which could click to expand or
        collapse related Contents.
        Collapsed: orange,
        Expanded: bisque
Content:
S(` `)L a normal palegreen plain text,
        1 line.

S(`!`)L a important bolder salmon plain text,
        1 line.

S(`>`)N
S(`=`)U   a bolder skyblue plain text N,
          1 line, which linked url is U. 
          those 2 lines are bound together.

S(`$`)N
S(`=`)U  N is alt text and title of image, 
         display under U,center align, 
         small, gray, 1 line.
         U is url of image, auto resize,
         but do not over 100% size,
         1 line, like div do.
         those 2 lines are bound together.

S(`@`)N
S(`|`)L
S(`|`)L
...
S(`|`)L   N is the PL name,
          display as burlywood, 1 line.
          all L in sequence 
          is n lines (n >= 1) codes of N,
          which can be click to copy,
          will be highlight if supported,
          or display as monospace plum.
          those lines are bound together.

S(`^`)L
S(`.`)L   first L is left, second is right,
          display as a line table like:
          left right
          with no borders but aligned,
          left salmon, right palegreen.
          those lines are bound together.
          if those appears continuous as T, 
          then aligned all of T as table,
          combinates the same left in T first,
          then the same right in T.
